course: dictionary
lesson: 3049
title: Finding east
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: East is one of the four compass points: north, east, south and west. East is the direction where the sun comes up in the morning, and it is opposite to west.
explain: On a map, east is on the right. Use this to check your directions: «In the morning the Sun is in the east, so shadows point west.» If you know where east is, you can work out where west is too.
explain: The word East can also mean a whole part of the world. When it has a capital E, it can mean the countries of Asia. «Simba» is a Swahili word, and Swahili is spoken in East Africa.
fact: East is the direction where the sun comes up in the morning.
fact: East is opposite to west, so if you face east, west is behind you.
fact: On a map, east is on the right.
fact: In the evening, shadows point east, because the sun is in the west.
fact: Longitude measures how far east or west a place is from the prime meridian, which runs through Greenwich in London.
exercise: «In the morning the Sun is in the east.» In the morning, which way do shadows point? | East | North | South | *West
exercise: A frog starts at a spot. It hops 6 steps east, then 2 steps west. How many steps east of the start is it now? | 2 | 8 | 6 | *4
exercise: On a map, which way is east? | Up | Down | Left | *Right
test: «Simba means lion in Swahili, a language of East Africa.» Which part of Africa does Swahili come from? | *East Africa | South Africa | West Africa | North Africa
test: A sign says «head east». Which way should you walk? | *Towards where the sun comes up | Towards the top of the map | Towards where the sun goes down | Towards the bottom of the map
exam: Longitude measures how far east or west a place is from the prime meridian. What does longitude measure? | *How far east or west a place is | How hot a place is | How high a mountain is | How far north or south a place is
